{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBRDeYkcNKnJYrwthxvv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted **index 24** (Pb 0.31 / Sb 0.69). It had the highest efficiency (EQE) of the three compositions I measured, at **0.039%**.\n\n**What the X-ray diffraction (XRD) scans showed:** there are two main phases along the composition line.\n- **Phase A** dominates the Sb-rich end and is almost pure at index 24.\n- **Phase B** dominates the Pb-rich end. At index 0 it also shows peaks that look like a PbO impurity.\n\n**Efficiency results (all 3 measurements used):**\n\n| Index | Pb / Sb | Phases | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 24 | 0.31 / 0.69 | nearly pure A | **0.0392** |\n| 15 | 0.49 / 0.51 | A + B mixed | 0.0360 |\n| 4 | 0.68 / 0.32 | mostly B | 0.0139 |\n\nEfficiency went up as the share of phase A increased, so phase A is the likely active material.\n\nWith only three measurements, I couldn't test the most Sb-rich compositions (indices 25–29). I used the last measurement on the Pb-rich side instead, to rule it out. Because the trend rises toward Sb, one of those could beat index 24. The 24 vs. 15 gap is also small (0.039% vs. 0.036%), so the peak in efficiency isn't pinned down. I used 4 of the 5 XRD scans."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":9228,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":558},"output_tokens":489,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aab74fbe-6035-4401-9c70-88fcfd82a0aa","uuid":"5212855d-c62e-4f6c-a504-e6fee438b961","timestamp":"2026-09-18T18:59:02.958Z","request_id":"req_011CfBRDe2k9y8FNdjkWS2qk"}
